{"id":"mahabharata-13-023","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":23,"title":"त्रयोविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 23 · Who is a worthy recipient","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks whom the brahmins call a fit recipient of gifts, the brahmin who bears the signs or the one who does not. Bhishma replies that conduct and learning, not the mark, make the worthy, and tells how a thousand horse-sacrifices were weighed against truth, and that a king should honour a good brahmin even from afar.","kn":"ದಾನಕ್ಕೆ ಯೋಗ್ಯನಾರೆಂದು, ಚಿಹ್ನೆಯುಳ್ಳ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣನೋ ಇಲ್ಲದವನೋ ಎಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಚಿಹ್ನೆಯಲ್ಲ ನಡತೆ-ವಿದ್ಯೆಯೇ ಯೋಗ್ಯನನ್ನಾಗಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಸಾವಿರ ಅಶ್ವಮೇಧ ಸತ್ಯದೊಡನೆ ತೂಗಿದ ಕಥೆ ಹೇಳಿ ಒಳ್ಳೆಯ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣನನ್ನು ದೂರದಿಂದಲೂ ಗೌರವಿಸಬೇಕೆಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर पूछते हैं कि दान का योग्य पात्र किसे कहा गया है, चिह्नधारी ब्राह्मण को या बिना चिह्न वाले को। भीष्म कहते हैं कि चिह्न नहीं बल्कि आचरण और विद्या पात्र बनाती है, वे हजार अश्वमेध को सत्य के साथ तौले जाने की कथा कहते हैं और कहते हैं कि राजा को योग्य ब्राह्मण का दूर से भी सम्मान करना चाहिए।","te":"దానానికి యోగ్య పాత్రుడెవరు, చిహ్నం గల బ్రాహ్మణుడా లేనివాడా అని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు. చిహ్నం కాదు, ప్రవర్తన, విద్య పాత్రుని చేస్తాయని, వేయి అశ్వమేధాలను సత్యంతో తూచిన కథ చెప్పి మంచి బ్రాహ్మణుని దూరం నుండైనా గౌరవించాలని భీష్ముడు అంటాడు.","ta":"தானத்துக்குத் தகுதியானவர் யார், அடையாளம் உடைய அந்தணனா இல்லாதவனா என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, அடையாளம் அல்ல, நடத்தையும் கல்வியுமே தகுதியாக்குகின்றன என்றும் ஆயிரம் அசுவமேதங்கள் உண்மையுடன் நிறுத்துப் பார்க்கப்பட்ட கதையையும் கூறி நல்ல அந்தணனை தூரத்திலிருந்தும் மதிக்க வேண்டும் என்று பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார்.","ml":"ബ്രാഹ്മണർ ദാനത്തിന് യോഗ്യനായ സ്വീകർത്താവെന്ന് വിളിക്കുന്നത് അടയാളങ്ങളുള്ളവനെയോ അവയില്ലാത്തവനെയോ എന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. സദാചാരവും പഠനവുമാണ്, അടയാളമല്ല, യോഗ്യനെ ഉണ്ടാക്കുന്നതെന്ന് ഭീഷ്മർ മറുപടി പറയുന്നു. ആയിരം അശ്വമേധയാഗങ്ങളെ സത്യത്തിനെതിരെ തൂക്കിനോക്കിയ കഥയും, നല്ല ബ്രാഹ്മണനെ ദൂരെനിന്നുപോലും രാജാവ് ആദരിക്കണമെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.23; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"किमाहुर्भरतश्रेष्ठ पात्रं विप्राः सनातनम् ।\nब्राह्मणं लिङ्गिनं चैव ब्राह्मणं वाप्यलिङ्गिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of the Bharatas, whom do the brahmins call an eternal worthy recipient: a brahmin who wears the outward marks or one who does not?"}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"स्ववृत्तिमभिपन्नाय लिङ्गिने वेतराय वा ।\nदेयमाहुर्महाराज उभावेतौ तपस्विनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, they say a gift may be given to one who has taken to his own livelihood, whether marked or unmarked; both of these are ascetics."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"श्रद्धया परया पूतो यः प्रयच्छेद्द्विजातये ।\nहव्यं कव्यं तथा दानं को दोषः स्यात्पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Grandfather, what fault is there if one purified by supreme faith gives offerings to the gods, offerings to the ancestors, or gifts to a twice-born?"}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"श्रद्धापूतो नरस्तात दुर्दान्तोऽपि न संशयः ।\nपूतो भवति सर्वत्र किं पुनस्त्वं महीपते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear one, a man purified by faith is purified everywhere, even if he is badly restrained, without doubt; how much more you, lord of the earth."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"न ब्राह्मणं परीक्षेत दैवेषु सततं नरः ।\nकव्यप्रदाने तु बुधाः परीक्ष्यं ब्राह्मणं विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should not examine a brahmin when making offerings to the gods; but the wise know that a brahmin should be examined when offerings to the ancestors are made."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"न ब्राह्मणः साधयते हव्यं दैवात्प्रसिध्यति ।\nदेवप्रसादादिज्यन्ते यजमाना न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is not the brahmin who makes the offering succeed; it succeeds through the divine. Sacrificers sacrifice by the gods' grace, without doubt."}},{"n":7,"text":"ब्राह्मणा भरतश्रेष्ठ सततं ब्रह्मवादिनः ।\nमार्कण्डेयः पुरा प्राह इह लोकेषु बुद्धिमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of the Bharatas, brahmins are always speakers of Brahman. The wise Markandeya long ago said so in these worlds."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":8,"text":"अपूर्वोऽप्यथ वा विद्वान्संबन्धी वाथ यो भवेत् ।\nतपस्वी यज्ञशीलो वा कथं पात्रं भवेत्तु सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whether he is unknown or learned or a relation, an ascetic or one devoted to sacrifice, how can he be a worthy recipient?"}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"कुलीनः कर्मकृद्वैद्यस्तथा चाप्यानृशंस्यवान् ।\nह्रीमानृजुः सत्यवादी पात्रं पूर्वे च ते त्रयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One of good family, a doer of rites, a physician, merciful, modest, upright and truthful: these are worthy recipients, and the earlier three as well."}},{"n":10,"text":"तत्रेदं शृणु मे पार्थ चतुर्णां तेजसां मतम् ।\nपृथिव्याः काश्यपस्याग्नेर्मार्कण्डेयस्य चैव हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear on this, Partha, the opinion of four radiant beings: Earth, Kashyapa, Fire and Markandeya."}},{"text":"पृथिव्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"The Earth said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"यथा महार्णवे क्षिप्तः क्षिप्रं लोष्टो विनश्यति ।\nतथा दुश्चरितं सर्वं त्रय्यावृत्त्या विनश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a clod thrown into the great ocean quickly dissolves, so all misconduct is dissolved by repeated study of the three Vedas."}},{"text":"काश्यप उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kashyapa said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"सर्वे च वेदाः सह षड्भिरङ्गैः\nसांख्यं पुराणं च कुले च जन्म ।\nनैतानि सर्वाणि गतिर्भवन्ति\nशीलव्यपेतस्य नरस्य राजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the Vedas with the six limbs, Sankhya, the Puranas and birth in a good family are not, king, a refuge for a man devoid of good character."}},{"text":"अग्निरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Fire said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"अधीयानः पण्डितं मन्यमानो\nयो विद्यया हन्ति यशः परेषाम् ।\nब्रह्मन्स तेनाचरते ब्रह्महत्यां\nलोकास्तस्य ह्यन्तवन्तो भवन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"A student who thinks himself learned and destroys the fame of others with his learning, brahmin, thereby commits the killing of a brahmin, and his worlds come to an end."}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"अश्वमेधसहस्रं च सत्यं च तुलया धृतम् ।\nनाभिजानामि यद्यस्य सत्यस्यार्धमवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not know of anyone who would obtain even half the fruit of truth when a thousand horse sacrifices and truth are weighed in a balance."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा ते जग्मुराशु चत्वारोऽमिततेजसः ।\nपृथिवी काश्यपोऽग्निश्च प्रकृष्टायुश्च भार्गवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, those four of boundless radiance quickly departed: Earth, Kashyapa, Fire and the long-lived descendant of Bhrigu."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"यदिदं ब्राह्मणा लोके व्रतिनो भुञ्जते हविः ।\nभुक्तं ब्राह्मणकामाय कथं तत्सुकृतं भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When brahmins in the world keeping vows eat the offering, how does a meal eaten for the sake of a brahmin become a merit?"}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"आदिष्टिनो ये राजेन्द्र ब्राह्मणा वेदपारगाः ।\nभुञ्जते ब्रह्मकामाय व्रतलुप्ता भवन्ति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"King of kings, brahmins who are masters of the Vedas, if they eat appointed offerings merely out of desire for the Brahmin's favor, are those whose vows are broken."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"अनेकान्तं बहुद्वारं धर्ममाहुर्मनीषिणः ।\nकिं निश्चितं भवेत्तत्र तन्मे ब्रूहि पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise say dharma is not fixed and has many doors. What is settled in it? Tell me, Grandfather."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"अहिंसा सत्यमक्रोध आनृशंस्यं दमस्तथा ।\nआर्जवं चैव राजेन्द्र निश्चितं धर्मलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Non-violence, truth, freedom from anger, kindness, self-control and straightforwardness, king of kings, are the settled marks of dharma."}},{"n":20,"text":"ये तु धर्मं प्रशंसन्तश्चरन्ति पृथिवीमिमाम् ।\nअनाचरन्तस्तद्धर्मं संकरे निरताः प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who go about this earth praising dharma without practicing it, delighted in confusion, lord,"}},{"n":21,"text":"तेभ्यो रत्नं हिरण्यं वा गामश्वान्वा ददाति यः ।\nदश वर्षाणि विष्ठां स भुङ्क्ते निरयमाश्रितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"whoever gives them jewels, gold, cows or horses lives in hell, eating filth for ten years."}},{"n":22,"text":"मेदानां पुल्कसानां च तथैवान्तावसायिनाम् ।\nकृतं कर्माकृतं चापि रागमोहेन जल्पताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They speak of what has been done and not done out of passion and confusion; so too for the Medas, Pulkasas and the lowest outcastes."}},{"n":23,"text":"वैश्वदेवं च ये मूढा विप्राय ब्रह्मचारिणे ।\nददतीह न राजेन्द्र ते लोकान्भुञ्जतेऽशुभान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fools who here do not give the Vaishvadeva offering to a celibate brahmin, king of kings, enjoy inauspicious worlds."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":24,"text":"किं परं ब्रह्मचर्यस्य किं परं धर्मलक्षणम् ।\nकिं च श्रेष्ठतमं शौचं तन्मे ब्रूहि पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"What is the highest part of celibacy, what is the highest mark of dharma, and what is the best purity? Tell me, Grandfather."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"ब्रह्मचर्यं परं तात मधुमांसस्य वर्जनम् ।\nमर्यादायां स्थितो धर्मः शमः शौचस्य लक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear one, the highest celibacy is abstaining from honey and meat; dharma is standing within limits; and tranquillity is the sign of purity."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"कस्मिन्काले चरेद्धर्मं कस्मिन्कालेऽर्थमाचरेत् ।\nकस्मिन्काले सुखी च स्यात्तन्मे ब्रूहि पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"At what time should one practice dharma, at what time pursue wealth, and at what time be happy? Tell me, Grandfather."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":27,"text":"काल्यमर्थं निषेवेत ततो धर्ममनन्तरम् ।\nपश्चात्कामं निषेवेत न च गच्छेत्प्रसङ्गिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should attend to wealth in the early part of the day, then to dharma next, and later to pleasure, and one should not become over-attached to it."}},{"n":28,"text":"ब्राह्मणांश्चाभिमन्येत गुरूंश्चाप्यभिपूजयेत् ।\nसर्वभूतानुलोमश्च मृदुशीलः प्रियंवदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should respect brahmins and honor teachers, be agreeable to all beings, gentle in nature and pleasant in speech."}},{"n":29,"text":"अधिकारे यदनृतं राजगामि च पैशुनम् ।\nगुरोश्चालीककरणं समं तद्ब्रह्महत्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"A lie told in office, slander carried to the king, and falsifying a teacher's words are equal to killing a brahmin."}},{"n":30,"text":"प्रहरेन्न नरेन्द्रेषु न गां हन्यात्तथैव च ।\nभ्रूणहत्यासमं चैतदुभयं यो निषेवते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should not strike kings, nor kill a cow; whoever commits either is like a killer of an embryo."}},{"n":31,"text":"नाग्निं परित्यजेज्जातु न च वेदान्परित्यजेत् ।\nन च ब्राह्मणमाक्रोशेत्समं तद्ब्रह्महत्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should never abandon the fire or abandon the Vedas, nor should one abuse a brahmin; that is the same as killing a brahmin."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":32,"text":"कीदृशाः साधवो विप्राः केभ्यो दत्तं महाफलम् ।\nकीदृशानां च भोक्तव्यं तन्मे ब्रूहि पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"What sort of brahmins are good, to whom are gifts greatly fruitful, and what sort of people should be fed? Tell me, Grandfather."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":33,"text":"अक्रोधना धर्मपराः सत्यनित्या दमे रताः ।\nतादृशाः साधवो विप्रास्तेभ्यो दत्तं महाफलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those free of anger, devoted to dharma, always truthful and fond of self-control are good brahmins; gifts to them bear great fruit."}},{"n":34,"text":"अमानिनः सर्वसहा दृष्टार्था विजितेन्द्रियाः ।\nसर्वभूतहिता मैत्रास्तेभ्यो दत्तं महाफलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who are without pride, tolerant of all, who see the purpose of things, with senses conquered, kind to all beings and friendly: gifts to them bear great fruit."}},{"n":35,"text":"अलुब्धाः शुचयो वैद्या ह्रीमन्तः सत्यवादिनः ।\nस्वकर्मनिरता ये च तेभ्यो दत्तं महाफलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who are not greedy, are pure, learned, modest, truthful and devoted to their own duties: gifts to them bear great fruit."}},{"n":36,"text":"साङ्गांश्च चतुरो वेदान्योऽधीयीत द्विजर्षभः ।\nषड्भ्यो निवृत्तः कर्मभ्यस्तं पात्रमृषयो विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A best of brahmins who studies the four Vedas with their limbs and has withdrawn from six actions, the sages know to be a worthy recipient."}},{"n":37,"text":"ये त्वेवंगुणजातीयास्तेभ्यो दत्तं महाफलम् ।\nसहस्रगुणमाप्नोति गुणार्हाय प्रदायकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gifts to those of such qualities bear great fruit; one who gives to a worthy one of good qualities receives a thousandfold."}},{"n":38,"text":"प्रज्ञाश्रुताभ्यां वृत्तेन शीलेन च समन्वितः ।\nतारयेत कुलं कृत्स्नमेकोऽपीह द्विजर्षभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A best of brahmins endowed with wisdom, learning, conduct and character can alone carry his whole family across."}},{"n":39,"text":"गामश्वं वित्तमन्नं वा तद्विधे प्रतिपादयेत् ।\nद्रव्याणि चान्यानि तथा प्रेत्यभावे न शोचति ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should give cows, horses, wealth, food and other goods to such a person; then one does not grieve in the afterlife."}},{"n":40,"text":"तारयेत कुलं कृत्स्नमेकोऽपीह द्विजोत्तमः ।\nकिमङ्ग पुनरेकं वै तस्मात्पात्रं समाचरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even one excellent brahmin can carry a whole family across; how much more if there is one more? Therefore one should act toward a worthy recipient."}},{"n":41,"text":"निशम्य च गुणोपेतं ब्राह्मणं साधुसंमतम् ।\nदूरादानाययेत्कृत्ये सर्वतश्चाभिपूजयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having learned of a brahmin of good qualities and approved by the good, one should invite him from afar for the rite and honor him in every way."}}]}]}